msgid "Explicit user stack and user DATA/BSS; data mappings are XN"
msgstr "Explicit user stack and user DATA/BSS; data mappings are XN"

msgid "The actual reset path must validate the exact part/security identity before copying user DATA and zeroing user BSS from the strong linker spans. The new bounded initializer validates every range before any store. Ordinary vendor startup still initializes privileged DATA/BSS; no runtime linker or pathname-based partition substitutes for this normal graph. The assembly does not select SRAM4 or the baremetal Stop2 owners."
msgstr "The actual reset path must validate the exact part/security identity before copying user DATA and zeroing user BSS from the strong linker spans. The new bounded initializer validates every range before any store. Ordinary vendor startup still initializes privileged DATA/BSS; no runtime linker or pathname-based partition substitutes for this normal graph. The assembly does not select SRAM4 or the baremetal Stop2 owners."

msgid "Bind the one trusted authority"
msgstr "Bind the one trusted authority"

msgid "Use the declarations in the [authority header](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/os/freertos/include/nexus/os/freertos_mpu_gpio.h), [protected task header](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/os/freertos/include/nexus/os/freertos_mpu.h) and [user entry header](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/os/freertos/include/nexus/os/freertos_user.h). Define exactly one immutable `nx_freertos_mpu_gpio_binding` in privileged Flash. It names a disjoint privileged-RAM task/control pair and a read-only grant. The grant names the read-only generated `nx_binding_led` pointer slot, logical LED device and mask `0x80`; it never accepts a user pointer as authority."
msgstr "Use the declarations in the [authority header](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/os/freertos/include/nexus/os/freertos_mpu_gpio.h), [protected task header](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/os/freertos/include/nexus/os/freertos_mpu.h) and [user entry header](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/os/freertos/include/nexus/os/freertos_user.h). Define exactly one immutable `nx_freertos_mpu_gpio_binding` in privileged Flash. It names a disjoint privileged-RAM task/control pair and a read-only grant. The grant names the read-only generated `nx_binding_led` pointer slot, logical LED device and mask `0x80`; it never accepts a user pointer as authority."

msgid "Before reading nested fields, the implementation checks full object extents, alignment and the five linked ranges: binding, grant, pointer slot, face and ops must fit privileged Flash; task, control and the complete concrete provider context must fit disjoint privileged RAM. The SoC validator requires the actual initialized GPIOC PC7 output provider and exact ops identity. Metadata bounds do not themselves prove every instruction's MPU permissions: the final normal ELF must also place the complete helper/provider function extents in privileged Flash."
msgstr "Before reading nested fields, the implementation checks full object extents, alignment and the five linked ranges: binding, grant, pointer slot, face and ops must fit privileged Flash; task, control and the complete concrete provider context must fit disjoint privileged RAM. The SoC validator requires the actual initialized GPIOC PC7 output provider and exact ops identity. Metadata bounds do not themselves prove every instruction's MPU permissions: the final normal ELF must also place the complete helper/provider function extents in privileged Flash."

msgid "One privileged lifecycle owner serializes task start/delete and authority open/close/join. Binding, grant, task metadata, control and provider remain valid for the linked image lifetime; open through join also forbids GPIO stop or reconfiguration. Only cold startup zero-initializes the metadata. The task's monotonic epoch survives deletion; join clears only the captured task epoch. Task-epoch wrap rejects rather than reusing an incarnation. NMI, HardFault, DMA and another security world never write these objects."
msgstr "One privileged lifecycle owner serializes task start/delete and authority open/close/join. Binding, grant, task metadata, control and provider remain valid for the linked image lifetime; open through join also forbids GPIO stop or reconfiguration. Only cold startup zero-initializes the metadata. The task's monotonic epoch survives deletion; join clears only the captured task epoch. Task-epoch wrap rejects rather than reusing an incarnation. NMI, HardFault, DMA and another security world never write these objects."

msgid "Enter through the real protected port"
msgstr "Enter through the real protected port"

msgid "Start the statically provided restricted task, then open the fixed authority before allowing its user calls. Open checks the actual live task handle equals its selected static TCB and snapshots that task epoch while pinning deletion. There is no caller-provided principal, lookup table or borrowed pointer argument."
msgstr "Start the statically provided restricted task, then open the fixed authority before allowing its user calls. Open checks the actual live task handle equals its selected static TCB and snapshots that task epoch while pinning deletion. There is no caller-provided principal, lookup table or borrowed pointer argument."

msgid "The user calls `nx_freertos_user_gpio_write(device, set, reset)`. Its real veneer enters SVC70 through the pinned protected call stack/origin checks. The dispatcher obtains the actual `xTaskGetCurrentTaskHandle()` before entering the saved-mask boundary, then rechecks open phase, live TCB/epoch, device and grant through the single real `nx_gpio_port_write()` effect. The selected provider performs exactly one bounded BSRR write. No kernel API, wait, allocation or product callback runs inside that effect boundary; the scalar result returns in R0."
msgstr "The user calls `nx_freertos_user_gpio_write(device, set, reset)`. Its real veneer enters SVC70 through the pinned protected call stack/origin checks. The dispatcher obtains the actual `xTaskGetCurrentTaskHandle()` before entering the saved-mask boundary, then rechecks open phase, live TCB/epoch, device and grant through the single real `nx_gpio_port_write()` effect. The selected provider performs exactly one bounded BSRR write. No kernel API, wait, allocation or product callback runs inside that effect boundary; the scalar result returns in R0."

msgid "Unknown device, wrong current task or bits outside `0x80` return PERMISSION. Zero combined masks or overlapping set/reset return INVALID; closed/stale incarnations return STATE; invalid privileged metadata returns INVALID; an unsupported context returns CONTEXT. These rejections perform no GPIO effect. READ, toggle, arbitrary pointers, user MMIO, DMA, IRQ and copied/asynchronous I/O are outside this API. Delay and tick-read remain separate services 6 and 13; the final ELF must prove all three Nexus user entries and their actual veneers are in the permitted execution regions."
msgstr "Unknown device, wrong current task or bits outside `0x80` return PERMISSION. Zero combined masks or overlapping set/reset return INVALID; closed/stale incarnations return STATE; invalid privileged metadata returns INVALID; an unsupported context returns CONTEXT. These rejections perform no GPIO effect. READ, toggle, arbitrary pointers, user MMIO, DMA, IRQ and copied/asynchronous I/O are outside this API. Delay and tick-read remain separate services 6 and 13; the final ELF must prove all three Nexus user entries and their actual veneers are in the permitted execution regions."

msgid "Lifecycle controls require privileged Thread and a scheduler that is running or not yet started, never suspended. FAULTMASK and BASEPRI must be zero except the selected port's canonical bootstrap BASEPRI before scheduler start. Service requires a running scheduler and zero BASEPRI. Incoming PRIMASK is saved and restored. This single-core exclusion is insufficient for an unmodeled writer; products must preserve the exact single-owner assumptions."
msgstr "Lifecycle controls require privileged Thread and a scheduler that is running or not yet started, never suspended. FAULTMASK and BASEPRI must be zero except the selected port's canonical bootstrap BASEPRI before scheduler start. Service requires a running scheduler and zero BASEPRI. Incoming PRIMASK is saved and restored. This single-core exclusion is insufficient for an unmodeled writer; products must preserve the exact single-owner assumptions."

msgid "Close, join and delete explicitly"
msgstr "Close, join and delete explicitly"

msgid "Close revokes new effects but retains the task pin. Join requires closed state and the same live incarnation, enters the saved-mask exclusion, removes the pin and detaches the authority's handle/task epoch. No scalar effect can straddle that single-core boundary. Join does not delete the task, stop GPIO or reset the task lifetime epoch. A failed close/join retains the obligation and storage."
msgstr "Close revokes new effects but retains the task pin. Join requires closed state and the same live incarnation, enters the saved-mask exclusion, removes the pin and detaches the authority's handle/task epoch. No scalar effect can straddle that single-core boundary. Join does not delete the task, stop GPIO or reset the task lifetime epoch. A failed close/join retains the obligation and storage."

msgid "Task deletion while pinned returns BUSY. After join, the lifecycle owner may delete the other task; self-delete is rejected. A protected closing marker is set before the real kernel deletion outside the IRQ guard, preventing reopen during deletion. The owner then clears the handle under a second guard while preserving the task epoch. Products still own user quiescence, task stack lifetime, scheduler startup, safe outputs and eventual provider/platform stop."
msgstr "Task deletion while pinned returns BUSY. After join, the lifecycle owner may delete the other task; self-delete is rejected. A protected closing marker is set before the real kernel deletion outside the IRQ guard, preventing reopen during deletion. The owner then clears the handle under a second guard while preserving the task epoch. Products still own user quiescence, task stack lifetime, scheduler startup, safe outputs and eventual provider/platform stop."

msgid "Evidence and remaining exits"
msgstr "Evidence and remaining exits"

msgid "Executable tests preceded production changes and exposed actual authority, task, provider-context and startup failures. The reviewed removal of an unexposed control counter retains the actual task epoch: its final model result is a behavior-preserving refactor GREEN, not a new behavioral RED. The maintained Native CMake target runs the final cases. Configuration and pinned-port checks retain default and unsupported-profile coverage. The [public consumer](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/cmake/package/verification/io_evolution/consumers/u575-mpu-gpio.c) uses the normal firmware graph, including real reset startup. The [source-bound evidence](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/testing/evidence/u575-mpu-gpio-20261020/README.md) records exact source phases, raw execution, compiled ABI facts, resources and the single relocated development-SDK consumer; it does not claim the complete current SDK transport plan passed."
msgstr "Executable tests preceded production changes and exposed actual authority, task, provider-context and startup failures. The reviewed removal of an unexposed control counter retains the actual task epoch: its final model result is a behavior-preserving refactor GREEN, not a new behavioral RED. The maintained Native CMake target runs the final cases. Configuration and pinned-port checks retain default and unsupported-profile coverage. The [public consumer](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/cmake/package/verification/io_evolution/consumers/u575-mpu-gpio.c) uses the normal firmware graph, including real reset startup. The [source-bound evidence](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/testing/evidence/u575-mpu-gpio-20261020/README.md) records exact source phases, raw execution, compiled ABI facts, resources and the single relocated development-SDK consumer; it does not claim the complete current SDK transport plan passed."

msgid "The selected ELF gate checks complete five-domain ranges, immutable authority pointers, protected objects, compiled task/control sizes, actual slots 6/13/70, three user wrappers and real veneers. Its explicit supported GNU Os startup shape checks actual reset/identity/user-initialization calls and DATA/BSS bounds; unrecognized shapes fail closed. These static layout, opcode and call facts do not execute protected SVC entry/exit. Runtime MPU faults, task switching, actual PC7 output, interrupt latency and HIL are not executed. The general IO-39/SOC-36 exits, other devices, multiple tasks/grants and M7 MPU remain open; a typed interface or host model does not close them."
msgstr "The selected ELF gate checks complete five-domain ranges, immutable authority pointers, protected objects, compiled task/control sizes, actual slots 6/13/70, three user wrappers and real veneers. Its explicit supported GNU Os startup shape checks actual reset/identity/user-initialization calls and DATA/BSS bounds; unrecognized shapes fail closed. These static layout, opcode and call facts do not execute protected SVC entry/exit. Runtime MPU faults, task switching, actual PC7 output, interrupt latency and HIL are not executed. The general IO-39/SOC-36 exits, other devices, multiple tasks/grants and M7 MPU remain open; a typed interface or host model does not close them."
